<%#
  The cookie notice, shared by every Vesopa website. Source and notes:
  shared/cookie-notice/ (run its sync.sh after changing it).

  First visit: the essentials are accepted straight away and a small notice
  slides up from the bottom, then hides itself. Every later visit shows
  nothing. The choice lives in a cookie and in localStorage under the key this
  site always used, so anybody who already chose is not asked again.

  The footer's "Cookie Settings" link (data-cc="open") reopens the switches.
  Optional scripts hang off `document.addEventListener('vesopa:consent', …)`.
%>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/vesopa-cookies.css">
<script src="/vesopa-cookies.js" data-policy="/cookies" defer></script>
